Work directly in the current hiyroscript/alva repository. First inspect the existing architecture, tests, documentation, and fighter definitions before modifying anything.

Objective

Implement one universal gameplay rule:

Every attack and every ability for every character must have a 0.5-second reuse wait. There are no character-specific exemptions.

The ONLY actions that must NOT receive this new 0.5-second wait are:

1. Normal run / left-right locomotion
2. Ground jump and all air jumps
3. Ground Shield
4. Air Deflect

Those four categories must preserve their current behavior.

Everything else that qualifies as an attack or actionable ability must obey the universal 0.5-second wait.

This rule must apply to the current roster, test fighters where applicable, and all future fighters automatically. Do not implement it by manually patching only #0001 and #0002.

⸻

What “0.5-second wait” means

Treat this as a reuse cooldown, NOT an added startup animation.

When an affected action is successfully accepted/started:

* that same action cannot successfully start again for 0.5 seconds;
* its existing startup, active, recovery, cast, animation, movement, hitbox, projectile, hit-cancel and other timings remain unchanged;
* do not insert 0.5 seconds of dead time before its animation or effect begins;
* do not delay damage/projectile release by 0.5 seconds;
* the cooldown runs in normal simulation time using the existing fixed-step timing model;
* 0.5 seconds at 60 Hz is 30 fixed steps;
* existing action commitment may make the practical time before reuse longer than 0.5 seconds. That is fine. Do not shorten an animation/recovery just to make the next use occur exactly at 0.5 seconds.

A press made while the cooldown is active must never start the action before the full 0.5 seconds have elapsed. Existing attack buffering may continue to work, provided the actual action does not begin early.

⸻

