Techniques

Every technique must have the same universal 0.5-second reuse wait.

This includes #0001’s current:

* Unlimited Void (attack4)
* Hollow Purple (attack5)

They currently have effectively no cooldown beyond their own cast/release commitment. That must change.

Their gameplay/animation timings must remain otherwise unchanged.

Summons

The repository supports summons even if the currently playable roster does not rely on one.

Summons must also obey the universal 0.5-second rule.

Do not leave the summon pathway using an arbitrary per-character cooldown that can bypass the universal rule.

Future summon characters must inherit the rule automatically.

Dash and air dash

Dash and air dash ARE affected.

Do not treat them as part of the “run” exemption.

The repo treats normal locomotion and Dash as distinct mechanics. The exemption is only normal run movement.

Therefore:

* grounded Dash must have a 0.5-second reuse wait;
* air dash must have a 0.5-second reuse wait;
* existing Energy costs, dash duration, dash cancel behavior, speed, momentum, available air-dash uses and animations remain unchanged.

Choose stable cooldown identifiers/state for these shared actions rather than fighter-specific hacks.

Combat Assist

Combat Assist must not bypass this rule.

If Combat Assist would approach a target before starting an attack, the attack must still be subject to the same 0.5-second availability check.

Do not allow Combat Assist to start or queue an approach in a way that lets the resulting attack bypass its cooldown.

Combat Assist should still ultimately use the same fighter/action rules as normal player input.

CPU

CPU-controlled fighters must obey exactly the same cooldowns.

Do not implement a separate CPU cooldown approximation.

The CPU already produces normal fighter inputs; preserve that architecture and make the fighter/shared combat layer authoritative.

If AI move selection currently considers cooldown readiness, update its readers as necessary so it does not deliberately spam unavailable actions.

⸻

The four exemptions

These are deliberate and must be tested.

1. Run

Normal horizontal movement must remain immediately responsive.

Do not:

* cooldown runLeft;
* cooldown runRight;
* stop directional steering because an offensive ability is cooling;
* introduce a universal “all input lock” that accidentally prevents running.

Dash is NOT covered by this exemption.

2. Jumps

Preserve all current jump behavior:

* ground jump
* high jump
* air jumps
* jump buffering
* coyote time
* jumping out of legal cancels where existing rules permit it

Do not give jumps the new 0.5-second reuse timer.

Existing limits such as the number of air jumps remain unchanged.

3. Ground Shield

The grounded Shield is exempt.

Do not add the universal 0.5-second reuse wait to:

* raising Shield;
* holding Shield;
* releasing and raising it again;
* perfect-Shield timing.

Keep its existing Energy/block rules and timing intact.

4. Air Deflect

Deflect is also completely exempt from the new rule.

This is especially important because ALVA internally represents Deflect as an attack created through createAttackDefinition.

Do NOT accidentally apply the offensive 0.5-second rule to Deflect simply because it uses the attack schema.

Preserve each Deflect’s existing behavior and authored timing/cooldown rules.

At the time of this task:

* #0001’s Deflect uses cooldown: 0;
* #0002’s Deflect uses cooldown: 0.05.

Those are defensive behavior and should NOT be normalized to 0.5.

createDeflectDefinition() must remain capable of creating an exempt Deflect without inheriting the universal offensive cooldown.

